---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import treeMark from '../../assets/brand/acaiaca-tree-mark-ivory.png';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { webPageStructuredData } from '../../lib/metadata';
import '../../styles/proposition-index.css';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Research Agenda — Proposition Index',
  description:
    'A selected public reference to Acaiaca propositions P4, P6, P8, and P11, with their current state, research role, public context, and provenance.',
  canonicalPath: '/research/agenda/',
};
const pageTitle = metadata.title + ' | Acaiaca Institute';
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={metadata.description}
  canonicalPath={metadata.canonicalPath}
  structuredData={webPageStructuredData(metadata)}
>
  <a class="agenda-skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="proposition-index-page">
    <section class="reference-hero" aria-labelledby="agenda-title">
      <div class="page-shell reference-hero-grid">
        <div class="reference-hero-main">
          <p class="eyebrow">Research reference</p>
          <h1 id="agenda-title">Research Agenda — Proposition Index</h1>
          <p class="reference-hero-lede">A selected public reference to propositions Acaiaca exposes across its research pages. Research Agenda v1.2 remains authoritative; this page makes those propositions understandable and inspectable without reproducing the internal Agenda.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="source-authority" aria-label="Source authority">
          <p class="source-authority-label">Source authority</p>
          <strong>Research Agenda v1.2</strong>
          <p>Canonical source for proposition identity, wording, formal state, and research role.</p>
          <p class="source-currentness">Selected public representation · September 2026</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="agenda-orientation" aria-labelledby="orientation-title">
      <div class="page-shell agenda-orientation-grid">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">How to read this page</p>
          <h2 id="orientation-title">Claims first. Identifiers second.</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="agenda-orientation-copy">
          <p>Each entry leads with the proposition’s human-readable meaning. Its stable proposition ID, formal state, research role, current public context, and provenance follow.</p>
          <div class="agenda-orientation-rule">
            <strong>This is a selective public index, not a complete rendering of Acaiaca’s Research Agenda.</strong>
            <p>P4, P6, P8, and P11 appear here because their identifiers are exposed by accepted public research pages. Additional propositions may be represented later when public need earns their inclusion.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="propositions-heading" aria-labelledby="propositions-title">
      <div class="page-shell propositions-heading-inner">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">Selected public propositions</p>
          <h2 id="propositions-title">Current proposition referents</h2>
        </header>
        <p>Each entry is independently addressable so a visitor arriving from another research page can understand the proposition without reading this page from the beginning.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proposition-entry" id="p4" aria-labelledby="p4-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="proposition-heading">
          <div class="proposition-heading-main">
            <p class="eyebrow">Selected proposition</p>
            <h2 id="p4-title">Responsibility becomes harder to justify coherently when practical control, decision authority, relevant understanding, and consequence-bearing are substantially separated across different actors.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="proposition-meta">
            <p class="proposition-id-state">P4 · Proposed</p>
            <p class="proposition-role">Foundational / inherited premise</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proposition-grid">
          <div class="proposition-body">
            <p>AI-mediated systems may increase the frequency or complexity of such separations.</p>
            <div class="proposition-explanation">
              <p class="proposition-explanation-label">Why it matters</p>
              <p>The proposition should be examined using established distinctions among moral responsibility, accountability, answerability, liability, causal contribution, and role responsibility.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="proposition-context" aria-label="P4 public context and provenance">
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Current public context</span>
              <a class="proposition-context-link" href="/research/current/">Current Research — Responsibility in AI-Mediated Systems →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Source</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Research Agenda v1.2</p>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Public representation</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Current as of September 2026</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proposition-entry" id="p6" aria-labelledby="p6-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="proposition-heading">
          <div class="proposition-heading-main">
            <p class="eyebrow">Selected proposition</p>
            <h2 id="p6-title">Increasing system capability does not necessarily increase human agency.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="proposition-meta">
            <p class="proposition-id-state">P6 · Proposed</p>
            <p class="proposition-role">Foundational / inherited premise</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proposition-grid">
          <div class="proposition-body">
            <p>Systems that increase what a person can accomplish may nevertheless diminish dimensions of practical agency such as understanding, influence, intervention, revocability, contestability, or exit, while also affecting related capacities such as retained competence.</p>
            <div class="proposition-explanation">
              <p class="proposition-explanation-label">Why it matters</p>
              <p>The open research concerns the conditions under which increased artificial capability increases, preserves, redistributes, or diminishes practical human agency.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="proposition-context" aria-label="P6 public context and provenance">
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Current public context</span>
              <a class="proposition-context-link" href="/research/human-ai-agency/">Explore Human–AI Agency →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Source</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Research Agenda v1.2</p>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Public representation</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Current as of September 2026</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proposition-entry" id="p8" aria-labelledby="p8-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="proposition-heading">
          <div class="proposition-heading-main">
            <p class="eyebrow">Selected proposition</p>
            <h2 id="p8-title">Under identifiable conditions, artificial assistance can improve human judgment performance without materially reducing practical agency.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="proposition-meta">
            <p class="proposition-id-state">P8 · Proposed</p>
            <p class="proposition-role">Open / integrative proposition</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proposition-grid">
          <div class="proposition-body">
            <p>The relevant conditions, tasks, forms of assistance, dimensions of judgment performance, and dimensions of practical agency remain subjects of inquiry.</p>
            <div class="proposition-explanation">
              <p class="proposition-explanation-label">Why it matters</p>
              <p>The proposition requires joint evaluation of performance and agency and may require longitudinal study where dependency, trust, skill retention, or changing delegation matter.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="proposition-context" aria-label="P8 public context and provenance">
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Current public context</span>
              <a class="proposition-context-link" href="/research/human-ai-agency/">Explore Human–AI Agency →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Source</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Research Agenda v1.2</p>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Public representation</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Current as of September 2026</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proposition-entry" id="p11" aria-labelledby="p11-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="proposition-heading">
          <div class="proposition-heading-main">
            <p class="eyebrow">Selected proposition</p>
            <h2 id="p11-title">Persistent AI systems may create sovereignty problems not fully addressed by conventional account ownership, application-level privacy controls, ordinary data portability, or isolated governance of individual state layers.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="proposition-meta">
            <p class="proposition-id-state">P11 · Proposed</p>
            <p class="proposition-role">Open / integrative proposition</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proposition-grid">
          <div class="proposition-body">
            <p>Existing research already addresses important parts of this problem through established privacy, identity, authorization, interoperability, memory, portability, preference, provenance, and governance mechanisms.</p>
            <div class="proposition-explanation">
              <p class="proposition-explanation-label">Why it matters</p>
              <p>The open research concerns whether the combined persistent state required for continuing delegated representation creates problems that cannot be resolved adequately by treating its component layers independently.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-qualification">
              <span>Narrowing / rejection condition</span>
              If existing mechanisms prove sufficient when properly integrated, the stronger sovereignty claim should be narrowed or rejected.
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="proposition-context" aria-label="P11 public context and provenance">
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Current public context</span>
              <a class="proposition-context-link" href="/research/digital-sovereignty/">Explore Digital Sovereignty →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Source</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Research Agenda v1.2</p>
            </div>
            <div class="proposition-context-item">
              <span class="proposition-context-label">Public representation</span>
              <p class="proposition-context-value">Current as of September 2026</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="agenda-public-note" aria-labelledby="public-note-title">
      <div class="page-shell agenda-public-note-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">About this public representation</p>
          <h2 id="public-note-title">Authority remains upstream.</h2>
          <p>Research Agenda v1.2 remains authoritative for proposition identity, canonical wording, formal state, and research role. This page is a visitor-facing representation of selected propositions rather than a second canonical Agenda.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="agenda-public-statement">The index may grow as additional proposition identifiers become publicly relevant. Future inclusion follows public need, not numerical completeness. The propositions shown here do not form a complete taxonomy, and this page does not expose Acaiaca’s internal maintenance-dependency graph.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="agenda-footer">
    <div class="page-shell agenda-footer-inner">
      <a class="agenda-footer-identity" href="/">
        <Image src={treeMark} alt="" width={28} height={28} />
        <span>Acaiaca Institute</span>
      </a>
      <p>Humanity is the loop.</p>
      <a href="/">Return to the Homepage</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>